{
  // GLASS AND WIRE - alternative rock.
  //
  // The trick this one is built on is loud-quiet-loud: verses that sit almost
  // as low as a ballad against choruses at nearly metal intensity, with nothing
  // in between. The dynamic range is the writing. Verse intensity is 0.30 and
  // chorus is 0.90, which is the widest gap in any of the presets.
  //
  // Triads rather than power chords, and the guitar plays sparse in the verses
  // - single held chords with air around them - then opens up for the chorus.
  // The bass carries the verses almost alone, which is where that sound comes
  // from in the first place.

